# Reflecting Mirror: "{X}, {T}: Change the target of target spell with a single target if that target is you. The new
# target must be a player. X is twice the mana value of that spell." X is defined by the text (CR 107.3c): it is not
# announced, and is determined with the total cost once the target spell is announced (CR 601.2f by way of 602.2b).
# Bot2 casts Braingeyser with X 1 (mana value 3 on the stack, CR 202.3e) at Bot1, then Lightning Bolt (mana value 1) at
# Bot1. Bot1 has four mana to pay with (Black Lotus and an untapped Mox): the Mirror can't target the Braingeyser, which
# would cost six (it would cost four if its X were not counted), but can target the Bolt for exactly two - Black Lotus's
# three blue leaves one. The Bolt's new target must be a player: Bot2's Ornithopter is a legal target for it but not
# offered, so Bot2, the only other player, is taken without a question (CR 115.7a). The Braingeyser still draws Bot1 a card.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Sol Ring
Reflecting Mirror
Black Lotus
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Braingeyser
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Island x10

